<h1 class="page-title">Master Thesis</h1>

<p>
    <br> Developed a decision-making framework for the strengthening and replacement of ageing concrete bridges, integrating structural reliability, service-life prediction, environmental impact, and cost. Through optimisation and multi-criteria analysis of CFRP, external prestressing, memory steel, UHPC, and replacement alternatives, the research demonstrated that CFRP is often the most effective and sustainable strengthening solution for shear-deficient prestressed concrete bridges.

